CORRECTED: Textual DFA for the preserved wc209 implementation.
Author: Jeon Sangeon, Assignment 1; retrospective documentation.

States: OUT_WORD (initial), IN_WORD, START_COM_OUT, START_COM_IN,
        IN_COM, END_COM.
Actions: C = increment characters, W = increment words.
Before each transition, increment nLine for a newline. For the first
input character only, initialize nLine to 1. Empty input stays at 0.

OUT_WORD:
  whitespace -> OUT_WORD; C
  /          -> START_COM_OUT; C
  otherwise  -> IN_WORD; C,W
IN_WORD:
  whitespace -> OUT_WORD; C
  /          -> START_COM_IN; C
  otherwise  -> IN_WORD; C
START_COM_OUT:
  whitespace -> OUT_WORD; C,W
  *          -> IN_COM; remember current nLine as err_line
  /          -> START_COM_IN; C,W
  otherwise  -> IN_WORD; C,W
START_COM_IN:
  whitespace -> OUT_WORD; C
  *          -> IN_COM; remember current nLine as err_line
  /          -> START_COM_IN; C
  otherwise  -> IN_WORD; C
IN_COM:
  *          -> END_COM
  newline    -> IN_COM; C
  otherwise  -> IN_COM
END_COM:
  /          -> OUT_WORD
  *          -> END_COM
  newline    -> IN_COM; C
  otherwise  -> IN_COM

EOF:
  START_COM_OUT -> W, then success
  IN_COM/END_COM -> stderr unterminated comment at err_line, failure
  other states -> success
A successful run prints nLine nWord nLetr followed by newline.
A read error is reported separately as a failure.

The slash counted upon entering a possible comment supplies the one
replacement-space character if the next character is '*'. A word for
that slash is deferred in START_COM_OUT until it is known not to open
a comment. Comment newlines are preserved, not discarded.
